// cases_a5.cla: A5Live (test-suite-review Task 13's own audit closure)
// -- exercises cg68k's `= inline a5` extern-clause codegen (cgCallExtA5,
// a bare `MOVE.L A5,D0`) inside a REAL booted program, the one thing
// testdata/cg68k/inline_a5.cla's own listing-diff test cannot do (that
// fixture pins the emitted bytes only -- it never runs, per its own doc
// comment: "UiCurrentA5 ... has no existing Clarus call site yet"). The
// runtime's own UiCurrentA5 (uiscript.cla) is declared but genuinely
// unreferenced from any Clarus call site (Task 13's `external func`
// sweep found it, alongside UiNewMenuStr, as the only two zero-call-site
// externs in runtime/clarus; UiNewMenuStr has since been deleted -- the
// language-runtime-cleanup phase, 2026-09-06 -- so UiCurrentA5 is now the
// only one left) -- this suite declares its OWN local extern
// against the same clause instead of wiring a real call site into
// uiscript.cla (out of this audit task's scope), same "user-code externs
// are the proven pattern" precedent cases_events.cla's own header comment
// already established for TbTickCount/TbMenuKey.
//
// A5 is fixed for a whole 68k application's run (the Mac app model's own
// "current A5" world-pointer register, restored by the OS around every
// event-loop callback) -- so the only real assertion available without
// tearing into QuickDraw-globals arithmetic is "nonzero and stable
// across two calls", which is still a genuine regression pin: a broken
// `cgCallExtA5` emission (wrong register, a stray push/pop unbalancing
// the two call sites' stack, garbage left in D0) would show up as either
// a null read or two calls disagreeing.
external func TbCurrentA5(): ptr = inline a5

func caseA5Live(): TestResult {
    var a: ptr
    var b: ptr
    var detail: string

    a = TbCurrentA5()
    b = TbCurrentA5()

    if a != ptr(0) and a == b {
        return tkPass("A5Live")
    }
    // Built up piecewise into `detail`, same native-68k per-statement
    // str/rec temp-slot budget reason as cases_events.cla's own cases.
    detail = "a " + tkIntToStr(int(a))
    detail = detail + " b " + tkIntToStr(int(b))
    return tkFail("A5Live", detail)
}
